<title>ITALY: Prodi and Juppe talk on Europe, but not on ERM.</title>
<headline>Prodi and Juppe talk on Europe, but not on ERM.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe said he and Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi held wide-ranging talks on European subjects but not concerning the re-entry of the lira to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM).</p>
<p>The French prime minister spoke to reporters after meeting Prodi and while in Rome attending the United Nations-sponsored World Food Summit.</p>
<p>Analysts believe that the lira will re-enter the European currency grid in the next few weeks after a four year absence.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
